UR<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">IrDA pulse width is 4/16 for OVS=0 and 4/8 for OVS=1. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_i2s_format_t<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-i2s-format-t\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-i2s-format-t\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>sl_hal_usart_i2s_format_t<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">I2S format selection. <\/p><table><tbody><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Enumerator<\/th><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">SL_HAL_USART_I2S_FORMAT_W32D32<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">32-bit word, 32-bit data. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">SL_HAL_USART_I2S_FORMAT_W32D24M<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">32-bit word, 32-bit data with 8 lsb masked. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">SL_HAL_USART_I2S_FORMAT_W32D24<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">32-bit word, 24-bit data. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">SL_HAL_USART_I2S_FORMAT_W32D16<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">32-bit word, 16-bit data. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">SL_HAL_USART_I2S_FORMAT_W32D8<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">32-bit word, 8-bit data. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">SL_HAL_USART_I2S_FORMAT_W16D16<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">16-bit word, 16-bit data. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">SL_HAL_USART_I2S_FORMAT_W16D8<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">16-bit word, 8-bit data. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">SL_HAL_USART_I2S_FORMAT_W8D8<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">8-bit word, 8-bit data. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_i2s_justify_t<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-i2s-justify-t\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-i2s-justify-t\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>sl_hal_usart_i2s_justify_t<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">I2S frame data justify. <\/p><table><tbody><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Enumerator<\/th><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">SL_HAL_USART_JUSTIFY_LEFT<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data is left-justified within the frame. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"fieldname\">SL_HAL_USART_JUSTIFY_RIGHT<\/td><td class=\"fielddescription\"><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data is right-justified within the frame. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><br><\/div><\/div><div class=\"def-class-section\"><h2>Function Documentation<span id=\"func-definition\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#func-definition\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h2><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_init_async<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-init-async\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-init-async\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_init_async (USART_TypeDef * usart, const <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/sl-hal-usart-async-init-t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_async_init_t<\/a> * init)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Initialize USART/UART for normal asynchronous mode. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>const <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/sl-hal-usart-async-init-t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_async_init_t<\/a> *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">init<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the initialization structure used to configure the basic async setup. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function will configure basic settings to operate in normal asynchronous mode.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">A special control setup not covered by this function must be done after using this function by direct modification of the CTRL register.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that pins used by the USART/UART module must be properly configured by the user explicitly for the USART/UART to work as intended. (When configuring pins, remember to consider the sequence of configuration to avoid unintended pulses/glitches on output pins.)<\/p><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_async_calculate_baudrate<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-async-calculate-baudrate\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-async-calculate-baudrate\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint32_t sl_hal_usart_async_calculate_baudrate (uint32_t ref_freq, uint32_t clk_div, <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-ovs-t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_ovs_t<\/a> ovs)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Calculate baudrate for USART/UART given reference frequency, clock division, and oversampling rate. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">ref_freq<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">USART/UART HF peripheral frequency used.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">clk_div<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A clock division factor to be used.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-ovs-t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_ovs_t<\/a><\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">ovs<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Oversample value of the USART.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function returns the baudrate that a USART/UART module will use if configured with the given frequency, clock divider, and mode. Notice that this function will not use the hardware configuration. It can be used to determine if a given configuration is sufficiently accurate for the application.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Baudrate with given settings. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_async_calculate_clock_div<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-async-calculate-clock-div\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-async-calculate-clock-div\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint32_t sl_hal_usart_async_calculate_clock_div (uint32_t ref_freq, uint32_t baudrate, <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-ovs-t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_ovs_t<\/a> ovs)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Calculate UART clock divider using given reference frequency, oversampling and baudrate. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">ref_freq<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Peripheral clock frequency.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">baudrate<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Transmission speed of the UART interface.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-ovs-t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_ovs_t<\/a><\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">ovs<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Oversampling rate.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">USART clock divider for desired baud rate. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_init_sync<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-init-sync\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-init-sync\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_init_sync (USART_TypeDef * usart, const <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/sl-hal-usart-sync-init-t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_sync_init_t<\/a> * init)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Initialize USART for synchronous mode. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART peripheral register block. (UART does not support this mode.)<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>const <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/sl-hal-usart-sync-init-t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_sync_init_t<\/a> *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">init<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the initialization structure used to configure basic async setup. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function will configure basic settings to operate in synchronous mode.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">A special control setup not covered by this function must be done after using this function by direct modification of the CTRL register.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that pins used by the USART module must be properly configured by the user explicitly for the USART to work as intended. (When configuring pins remember to consider the sequence of configuration to avoid unintended pulses/glitches on output pins.)<\/p><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_sync_calculate_baudrate<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-sync-calculate-baudrate\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-sync-calculate-baudrate\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint32_t sl_hal_usart_sync_calculate_baudrate (uint32_t ref_freq, uint32_t clk_div)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Calculate baudrate for USART/UART (sync mode) given reference frequency, clock division. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">ref_freq<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">USART/UART HF peripheral frequency used.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">clk_div<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A clock division factor to be used.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function returns the baudrate that a USART/UART module will use if configured with the given frequency, clock divider, and mode. Notice that this function will not use the hardware configuration. It can be used to determine if a given configuration is sufficiently accurate for the application.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Baudrate with given settings. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_sync_calculate_clock_div<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-sync-calculate-clock-div\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-sync-calculate-clock-div\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint32_t sl_hal_usart_sync_calculate_clock_div (uint32_t ref_freq, uint32_t baudrate)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Calculate UART (sync mode) clock divider using given reference frequency and baudrate. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">ref_freq<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Peripheral clock frequency.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">baudrate<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Transmission speed of the USART/UART interface.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">USART clock divider for desired baud rate. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_init_irda<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-init-irda\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-init-irda\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_init_irda (USART_TypeDef * usart, const <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/sl-hal-usart-irda-init-t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_irda_init_t<\/a> * init)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Initialize USART for asynchronous IrDA mode. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>const <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/sl-hal-usart-irda-init-t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_irda_init_t<\/a> *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">init<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the initialization structure used to configure async IrDA setup.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function will configure basic settings to operate in asynchronous IrDA mode.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">A special control setup not covered by this function must be done after using this function by direct modification of the CTRL and IRCTRL registers.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that pins used by the USART/UART module must be properly configured by the user explicitly for the USART/UART to work as intended. (When configuring pins, remember to consider the sequence of configuration to avoid unintended pulses/glitches on output pins.)<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Not all USART instances support IrDA. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_init_i2s<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-init-i2s\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-init-i2s\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_init_i2s (USART_TypeDef * usart, const <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/sl-hal-usart-i2s-init-t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_i2s_init_t<\/a> * init)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Initialize USART for I2S mode. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART peripheral register block. (UART does not support this mode.)<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>const <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/sl-hal-usart-i2s-init-t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_i2s_init_t<\/a> *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">init<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the initialization structure used to configure the basic I2S setup.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function will configure basic settings to operate in I2S mode.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">A special control setup not covered by this function must be done after using this function by direct modification of the CTRL and I2SCTRL registers.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that pins used by the USART module must be properly configured by the user explicitly for the USART to work as intended. (When configuring pins, remember to consider the sequence of configuration to avoid unintended pulses/glitches on output pins.)<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function does not apply to all USART's. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_reset<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-reset\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-reset\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_reset (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Reset USART/UART to the same state that it was in after a hardware reset. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to USART/UART peripheral register block. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_tx<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-tx\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-tx\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_tx (USART_TypeDef * usart, uint8_t data)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Transmit one 4-9 bit frame. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint8_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">data<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data to transmit. See details above for more information. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Depending on the frame length configuration, 4-8 (least significant) bits from <code>data<\/code> are transmitted. If the frame length is 9, 8 bits are transmitted from <code>data<\/code> and one bit as specified by CTRL register, BIT8DV field. See <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-tx-ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_tx_ext()<\/a> for transmitting 9 bit frame with full control of all 9 bits.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that possible parity/stop bits in asynchronous mode are not considered part of a specified frame bit length.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function will stall if the buffer is full until the buffer becomes available.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_spi_transfer<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-spi-transfer\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-spi-transfer\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint8_t sl_hal_usart_spi_transfer (USART_TypeDef * usart, uint8_t data)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Perform one 8 bit frame SPI transfer. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint8_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">data<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data to transmit.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function will stall if the transmit buffer is full. When a transmit buffer becomes available, data is written and the function will wait until data is fully transmitted. The SPI return value is then read out and returned.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data received. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_tx_double<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-tx-double\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-tx-double\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_tx_double (USART_TypeDef * usart, uint16_t data)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Transmit two 4-9 bit frames or one 10-16 bit frame. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint16_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">data<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data to transmit, the least significant byte holds the frame transmitted first. See details above for more info. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Depending on the frame length configuration, 4-8 (least significant) bits from each byte in <code>data<\/code> are transmitted. If frame length is 9, 8 bits are transmitted from each byte in <code>data<\/code> adding one bit as specified by the CTRL register, BIT8DV field, to each byte. See <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-tx-double-ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_tx_double_ext()<\/a> for transmitting two 9 bit frames with full control of all 9 bits.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">If the frame length is 10-16, 10-16 (least significant) bits from <code>data<\/code> are transmitted.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that possible parity/stop bits in asynchronous mode are not considered part of a specified frame bit length.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function will stall if the buffer is full until the buffer becomes available.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_tx_double_ext<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-tx-double-ext\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-tx-double-ext\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_tx_double_ext (USART_TypeDef * usart, uint32_t data)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Transmit two 4-9 bit frames or one 10-16 bit frame with extended control. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">data<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data to transmit with extended control. Contains two 16 bit words concatenated. Least significant word holds the frame transmitted first. If the frame length is 4-9, two frames with 4-9 least significant bits from each 16 bit word are transmitted.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that possible parity/stop bits in asynchronous mode are not considered part of a specified frame bit length.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function will stall if the buffer is full until the buffer becomes available.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">If the frame length is 10-16 bits, 8 data bits are taken from the least significant 16 bit word and the remaining bits from the other 16 bit word.<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Additional control bits are available as documented in the reference manual (set to 0 if not used). For 10-16 bit frame length, these control bits are taken from the most significant 16 bit word. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_tx_ext<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-tx-ext\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-tx-ext\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_tx_ext (USART_TypeDef * usart, uint16_t data)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Transmit one 4-9 bit frame with extended control. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint16_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">data<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data to transmit with extended control. Least significant bit contains frame bits. Additional control bits are available as documented in the reference manual (set to 0 if not used). <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that possible parity/stop bits in asynchronous mode are not considered part of a specified frame bit length.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function will stall if the buffer is full until the buffer becomes available.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_enable_rx_prs_trigger<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-enable-rx-prs-trigger\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-enable-rx-prs-trigger\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_enable_rx_prs_trigger (USART_TypeDef * usart, uint8_t channel)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable automatic enabling of reception using the PRS as a trigger. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to the USART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint8_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">channel<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">PRS channel to use. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_disable_rx_prs_trigger<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-disable-rx-prs-trigger\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-disable-rx-prs-trigger\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_disable_rx_prs_trigger (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disable automatic enabling of reception using the PRS as a trigger. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to the USART peripheral register block. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_enable_tx_prs_trigger<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-enable-tx-prs-trigger\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-enable-tx-prs-trigger\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_enable_tx_prs_trigger (USART_TypeDef * usart, uint8_t channel)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable automatic enabling of transmission using the PRS as a trigger. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to the USART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint8_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">channel<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">PRS channel number. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_disable_tx_prs_trigger<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-disable-tx-prs-trigger\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-disable-tx-prs-trigger\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_disable_tx_prs_trigger (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disable automatic enabling of transmission using the PRS as a trigger. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to the USART peripheral register block. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_async_set_clock_div<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-async-set-clock-div\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-async-set-clock-div\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_async_set_clock_div (USART_TypeDef * usart, uint32_t clock_div)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Set UART mode clock divider. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to the USART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">clock_div<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Clock divider value. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_async_get_clock_div<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-async-get-clock-div\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-async-get-clock-div\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint32_t sl_hal_usart_async_get_clock_div (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Get UART mode clock divider. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to the USART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Clock divider value. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_enable<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-enable\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-enable\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_enable (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable USART. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART peripheral register block. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_disable<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-disable\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-disable\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_disable (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disable USART. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART peripheral register block. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_enable_rx<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-enable-rx\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-enable-rx\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_enable_rx (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable USART receiver. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART peripheral register block. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_disable_rx<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-disable-rx\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-disable-rx\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_disable_rx (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disable USART receiver. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART peripheral register block. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_enable_tx<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-enable-tx\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-enable-tx\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_enable_tx (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable USART transmitter. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART peripheral register block. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_disable_tx<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-disable-tx\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-disable-tx\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_disable_tx (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disable USART transmitter. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART peripheral register block. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_clear_rx<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-clear-rx\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-clear-rx\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_clear_rx (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Clear RX FIFO. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to the USART peripheral register block. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_clear_tx<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-clear-tx\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-clear-tx\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_clear_tx (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Clear TX FIFO. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to the USART peripheral register block. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_rx<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-rx\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-rx\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint8_t sl_hal_usart_rx (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Receive one 4-8 bit frame, (or part of 10-16 bit frame). <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function is normally used to receive one frame when operating with frame length 4-8 bits. See <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-rx-ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_rx_ext()<\/a> for reception of 9 bit frames.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that possible parity/stop bits in asynchronous mode are not considered part of a specified frame bit length.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function will stall if the buffer is empty until data is received. Alternatively, the user can explicitly check whether data is available. If data is available, call <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-rx-data-get\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_rx_data_get()<\/a> to read the RXDATA register directly.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data received. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_rx_double<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-rx-double\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-rx-double\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint16_t sl_hal_usart_rx_double (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Receive two 4-8 bit frames or one 10-16 bit frame. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function is normally used to receive one frame when operating with frame length 10-16 bits. See <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-rx-double-ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_rx_double_ext()<\/a> for reception of two 9 bit frames.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that possible parity/stop bits in asynchronous mode are not considered part of a specified frame bit length.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function will stall if the buffer is empty until data is received. Alternatively, the user can explicitly check whether data is available. If data is available, call <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-rx-double-get\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_rx_double_get()<\/a> to read the RXDOUBLE register directly.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data received. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_rx_double_ext<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-rx-double-ext\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-rx-double-ext\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint32_t sl_hal_usart_rx_double_ext (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Receive two 4-9 bit frames, or one 10-16 bit frame with extended information. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function is normally used to receive one frame when operating with frame length 10-16 bits and additional RX status information is required.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that possible parity/stop bits in asynchronous mode are not considered part of a specified frame bit length.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function will stall if buffer is empty until data is received. Alternatively, the user can explicitly check whether data is available. If data is available, call <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-rx-double-x-get\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_rx_double_x_get()<\/a> to read the RXDOUBLEX register directly.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data received. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_rx_ext<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-rx-ext\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-rx-ext\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint16_t sl_hal_usart_rx_ext (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Receive one 4-9 bit frame (or part of 10-16 bit frame) with extended information. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function is normally used to receive one frame when operating with frame length 4-9 bits and additional RX status information is required.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that possible parity/stop bits in asynchronous mode are not considered part of a specified frame bit length.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function will stall if the buffer is empty until data is received. Alternatively, the user can explicitly check whether data is available. If data is available, call <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-rx-data-get\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_rx_data_get()<\/a> to read the RXDATAX register directly.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data received. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_rx_data_get<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-rx-data-get\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-rx-data-get\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint8_t sl_hal_usart_rx_data_get (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Receive one 4-8 bit frame, (or part of 10-16 bit frame). <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function is used to quickly receive one 4-8 bits frame by reading the RXDATA register directly, without checking the STATUS register for the RXDATAV flag. This can be useful from the RXDATAV interrupt handler, i.e., waiting is superfluous, in order to quickly read the received data. Please refer to <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-rx-ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_rx_ext()<\/a> for reception of 9 bit frames.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Because this function does not check whether the RXDATA register actually holds valid data, it should only be used in situations when it is certain that there is valid data, ensured by some external program routine, e.g., when handling an RXDATAV interrupt. The <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-rx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_rx()<\/a> is normally a better choice if the validity of the RXDATA register is not certain.<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that possible parity/stop bits in asynchronous mode are not considered part of specified frame bit length.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data received. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_rx_double_get<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-rx-double-get\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-rx-double-get\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint16_t sl_hal_usart_rx_double_get (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Receive two 4-8 bit frames, or one 10-16 bit frame. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function is used to quickly receive one 10-16 bits frame or two 4-8 bit frames by reading the RXDOUBLE register directly, without checking the STATUS register for the RXDATAV flag. This can be useful from the RXDATAV interrupt handler, i.e., waiting is superfluous, in order to quickly read the received data. This function is normally used to receive one frame when operating with frame length 10-16 bits. Please refer to <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-rx-double-x-get\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_rx_double_x_get()<\/a> for reception of two 9 bit frames.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Because this function does not check whether the RXDOUBLE register actually holds valid data, it should only be used in situations when it is certain that there is valid data, ensured by some external program routine, e.g., when handling an RXDATAV interrupt. The <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-rx-double\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_rx_double()<\/a> is normally a better choice if the validity of the RXDOUBLE register is not certain.<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that possible parity/stop bits in asynchronous mode are not considered part of specified frame bit length.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data received. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_rx_double_x_get<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-rx-double-x-get\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-rx-double-x-get\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint32_t sl_hal_usart_rx_double_x_get (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Receive two 4-9 bit frames, or one 10-16 bit frame with extended information. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function is used to quickly receive one 10-16 bits frame or two 4-9 bit frames by reading the RXDOUBLEX register directly, without checking the STATUS register for the RXDATAV flag. This can be useful from the RXDATAV interrupt handler, i.e., waiting is superfluous, in order to quickly read the received data.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Because this function does not check whether the RXDOUBLEX register actually holds valid data, it should only be used in situations when it is certain that there is valid data, ensured by some external program routine, e.g., when handling an RXDATAV interrupt. The <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-rx-double-ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_rx_double_ext()<\/a> is normally a better choice if the validity of the RXDOUBLEX register is not certain.<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that possible parity/stop bits in asynchronous mode are not considered part of specified frame bit length.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data received. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_rx_data_x_get<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-rx-data-x-get\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-rx-data-x-get\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint16_t sl_hal_usart_rx_data_x_get (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Receive one 4-9 bit frame, (or part of 10-16 bit frame) with extended information. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function is used to quickly receive one 4-9 bit frame, (or part of 10-16 bit frame) with extended information by reading the RXDATAX register directly, without checking the STATUS register for the RXDATAV flag. This can be useful from the RXDATAV interrupt handler, i.e., waiting is superfluous, in order to quickly read the received data.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Because this function does not check whether the RXDATAX register actually holds valid data, it should only be used in situations when it is certain that there is valid data, ensured by some external program routine, e.g., when handling an RXDATAV interrupt. The <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart#sl-hal-usart-rx-ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_hal_usart_rx_ext()<\/a> is normally a better choice if the validity of the RXDATAX register is not certain.<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Notice that possible parity/stop bits in asynchronous mode are not considered part of specified frame bit length.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Data received. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_clear_interrupts<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-clear-interrupts\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-clear-interrupts\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_clear_interrupts (USART_TypeDef * usart, uint32_t flags)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Clear one or more pending USART interrupts. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">flags<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pending USART/UART interrupt source(s) to clear. Use one or more valid interrupt flags for the USART module (USART_IF_nnn) OR'ed together. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_disable_interrupts<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-disable-interrupts\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-disable-interrupts\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_disable_interrupts (USART_TypeDef * usart, uint32_t flags)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disable one or more USART interrupts. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">flags<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">USART/UART interrupt source(s) to disable. Use one or more valid interrupt flags for the USART module (USART_IF_nnn) OR'ed together. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_enable_interrupts<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-enable-interrupts\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-enable-interrupts\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_enable_interrupts (USART_TypeDef * usart, uint32_t flags)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable one or more USART interrupts. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">flags<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">USART/UART interrupt source(s) to enable. Use one or more valid interrupt flags for the USART module (USART_IF_nnn) OR'ed together. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Depending on the use, a pending interrupt may already be set prior to enabling the interrupt. To ignore a pending interrupt, consider using USART_IntClear() prior to enabling the interrupt.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_get_pending_interrupts<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-get-pending-interrupts\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-get-pending-interrupts\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint32_t sl_hal_usart_get_pending_interrupts (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Get pending USART interrupt flags. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">The event bits are not cleared by the use of this function.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">USART/UART interrupt source(s) pending. Returns one or more valid interrupt flags for the USART module (USART_IF_nnn) OR'ed together. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_get_enabled_pending_interrupts<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-get-enabled-pending-interrupts\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-get-enabled-pending-interrupts\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint32_t sl_hal_usart_get_enabled_pending_interrupts (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Get enabled and pending USART interrupt flags. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Useful for handling more interrupt sources in the same interrupt handler.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Interrupt flags are not cleared by the use of this function.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Pending and enabled USART interrupt sources. The return value is the bitwise AND combination of<\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">the OR combination of enabled interrupt sources in USARTx_IEN_nnn register (USARTx_IEN_nnn) and<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">the OR combination of valid interrupt flags of the USART module (USARTx_IF_nnn). <\/p><\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_set_interrupts<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-set-interrupts\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-set-interrupts\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void sl_hal_usart_set_interrupts (USART_TypeDef * usart, uint32_t flags)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Set one or more pending USART interrupts from SW. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">flags<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">USART/UART interrupt source(s) to set to pending. Use one or more valid interrupt flags for the USART module(USART_IF_nnn) OR'ed together. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_hal_usart_get_status<span id=\"sl-hal-usart-get-status\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-hal-usart-get-status\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>uint32_t sl_hal_usart_get_status (USART_TypeDef * usart)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Get USART STATUS register. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>USART_TypeDef *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">usart<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A pointer to the USART/UART peripheral register block.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">STATUS register value. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><\/div><div class=\"def-class-section\"><h2>&nbsp;<\/h2><div><\/div><div><\/div><div><\/div><div><\/div><div><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/article><footer class=\"footer-commons-msg\"><\/footer><div class=\"light_theme hidden-lg\" ub-in-page=\"634f96f53042a864e44b82f8\"><\/div><div class=\"dark_theme hidden-lg\" ub-in-page=\"699fe6e9dac31e032209597c\"><\/div><div id=\"page-nav-buttons\" class=\"page-nav-buttons\"><\/div>","url":"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/5.2.2/platform-peripheral-efr32xg24/usart","status":"success"}
